IMPORT prelude

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- LAYER 1, part ssc6: the employer's duty to pay, as regulative rules (ss 151(1), 164(1) and (3),
-- 171ZA(1) and 171ZD(1), 171ZL(1) and 171ZM(1)).
--
-- Each Part makes the person liable bound to pay the statutory pay when the entitlement conditions
-- are met. The decision functions in ssc6-ssp, ssc6-smp, ssc6-spp and ssc6-sap say WHEN that is so
-- (`s 151(1) the employer is liable to make a payment of statutory sick pay in respect of the day`
-- and its counterparts); these rules say WHAT then falls due, and are the same relation seen
-- as a duty: the person entitled holds the claim, the person liable bears the duty (see NOTES.md,
-- Jural relations). They do not restate the conditions: a caller applies a rule below only after
-- the decision function answers `JUST TRUE`, and never when it answers `NOTHING`.
--
-- The text states no time limit and no consequence of non-payment in these provisions, so none is
-- written: no WITHIN, no LEST. The default of a MUST with no deadline is that nothing is breached
-- until the payment is made, and the trace shows the residual duty. The text does not say when
-- payment falls due.
-- A trace is run, not asserted: the stable binary prints a trace result as an Information message
-- and `check.sh` counts none, so each trace below has its expected result written beside it, and the
-- same duty is covered as a decision function and asserted there (NOTES.md, "What the stable binary
-- does not accept").
-- On the stable binary an input named in the action (the amount) is not compared with the payload of
-- the event, so a payment of any amount fulfils the duty; the amount is stated in the action so that
-- the duty reads as the section does.

§ `Statutory pay -- the person liable must pay`

DECLARE `s 151(1) Party to a statutory pay duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 151(1) the employer liable for statutory sick pay`
    `s 164(3) the person liable for statutory maternity pay`
    `s 171ZD(1) the person liable for statutory paternity pay`
    `s 171ZM(1) the person liable for statutory adoption pay`

DECLARE `s 151(1) Act under a statutory pay duty` IS ONE OF
    `s 151(1) pay statutory sick pay` HAS `the amount of statutory sick pay in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 164(1) pay statutory maternity pay` HAS `the amount of statutory maternity pay in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 171ZA(1) pay statutory paternity pay` HAS `the amount of statutory paternity pay in pounds` IS A NUMBER
    `s 171ZL(1) pay statutory adoption pay` HAS `the amount of statutory adoption pay in pounds` IS A NUMBER

-- Plain gloss: the employer pays the employee statutory sick pay for a day of incapacity for work.
-- src:3098 | (1) Where an employee has a day of incapacity for work in relation to his contract of service with an employer, that employer shall, if the conditions set out in sections 153 and 154 below are satisfied, be liable to make him, in accordance with the following provisions of this Part of this Act, a payment (to be known as “statutory sick pay”) in respect of that day.
@ref s 151(1) (src:3098)
GIVEN `the amount of statutory sick pay for the day in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 151(1) Party to a statutory pay duty` `s 151(1) Act under a statutory pay duty`
`s 151(1) the employer's duty to pay statutory sick pay for the day` MEANS
    PARTY `s 151(1) the employer liable for statutory sick pay`
    MUST `s 151(1) pay statutory sick pay` `the amount of statutory sick pay for the day in pounds`

-- Plain gloss: the person liable pays the woman statutory maternity pay.
-- src:3243 | (1) Where a woman who is or has been an employee satisfies the conditions set out in this section, she shall be entitled, in accordance with the following provisions of this Part of this Act, to payments to be known as “statutory maternity pay”.
-- src:3248 | (3) The liability to make payments of statutory maternity pay to a woman is a liability of any person of whom she has been an employee as mentioned in subsection (2)(a) above.
@ref s 164(1), s 164(3) (src:3243) (src:3248)
GIVEN `the amount of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 151(1) Party to a statutory pay duty` `s 151(1) Act under a statutory pay duty`
`s 164(3) the duty to pay statutory maternity pay for the week` MEANS
    PARTY `s 164(3) the person liable for statutory maternity pay`
    MUST `s 164(1) pay statutory maternity pay` `the amount of statutory maternity pay for the week in pounds`

-- Plain gloss: the person liable pays the man statutory paternity pay.
-- src:3388 | (1) Where a person satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) below, he shall be entitled in accordance with the following provisions of this Part to payments to be known as “statutory paternity pay”.
-- src:3444 | (1) The liability to make payments of ... statutory paternity pay under section 171ZA or 171ZB above is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments has been an employee as mentioned in subsection (2)(b) and (d) of that section.
@ref s 171ZA(1), s 171ZD(1) (src:3388) (src:3444)
GIVEN `the amount of statutory paternity pay for the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 151(1) Party to a statutory pay duty` `s 151(1) Act under a statutory pay duty`
`s 171ZD(1) the duty to pay statutory paternity pay for the week` MEANS
    PARTY `s 171ZD(1) the person liable for statutory paternity pay`
    MUST `s 171ZA(1) pay statutory paternity pay` `the amount of statutory paternity pay for the week in pounds`

-- Plain gloss: the person liable pays the person statutory adoption pay.
-- src:3561 | (1) Where a person who is, or has been, an employee satisfies the conditions in subsection (2) below, he shall be entitled in accordance with the following provisions of this Part to payments to be known as “statutory adoption pay”.
-- src:3612 | (1) The liability to make payments of statutory adoption pay is a liability of any person of whom the person entitled to the payments has been an employee as mentioned in section 171ZL(2)(b) above.
@ref s 171ZL(1), s 171ZM(1) (src:3561) (src:3612)
GIVEN `the amount of statutory adoption pay for the week in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 151(1) Party to a statutory pay duty` `s 151(1) Act under a statutory pay duty`
`s 171ZM(1) the duty to pay statutory adoption pay for the week` MEANS
    PARTY `s 171ZM(1) the person liable for statutory adoption pay`
    MUST `s 171ZL(1) pay statutory adoption pay` `the amount of statutory adoption pay for the week in pounds`

-- Traces. Expected result beside each (written from the text: a MUST with no WITHIN is not breached
-- while the payment is outstanding, and the payment fulfils it).

-- Expected: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 151(1) the employer's duty to pay statutory sick pay for the day` 24.65 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `s 151(1) the employer liable for statutory sick pay` DOES `s 151(1) pay statutory sick pay` 24.65 AT 5

-- Expected: the duty stands, unbreached (no deadline is stated)
#TRACE `s 151(1) the employer's duty to pay statutory sick pay for the day` 24.65 AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 400)

